@DarkMarc. ⁠archived-foundation-room⁠

If I got this right, I think that by "wallet abstraction" they mean that players won't notice they are playing a web3 game. You basically aren't required to sign any transactions, and you don't pay any fees upfront. Once you want to play the "real decentralized game" you will need to set up your Solana Wallet, and then you can migrate all of your assets to that wallet. You can think of it as a CEX account, and then you can move your assets off into a non-custodial wallet.
That being said, you will still consume R4s and everything else. It doesn't change what you do, but how you do it. The on-chain mechanics are fully transparent with wallet abstraction.

@SW4GN3R why the buff to SDUs when we were just talking about how its the easiest game loop in the game currently?  E.g. you can set your fleet once and come back in a month.

With more SDUS, they will be now be cheaper, which means more will be installed into the LP system.  This will further dilute LP rewards from those who are mining/upgrading with components.  Mining/upgrade LP rewards have already taken a 30-50% hit because people are mass buying SDUs from the market, installing them for 1-3% profit, and causing mass dilution via the diminishing returns of the LP system.   Players are taking that 1% profit and causing the entire pool to loose 20-30%.   Feels like this will make it worse.

At least this is what I'm personally seeing and what we are seeing in Oni right now.  I don't have the econ data but any insight would be appreciated.

